{"requirements":[{"id":"recovered_eod3","requirement":"Reconstruct the recovered tree from the base and ordered change archives so it represents end of day 3, including deletions and latest file versions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The archives and deletion manifests were inspected, then applied in chain order. Final verification directly matched dispatch.txt to day3.tar and retain.txt to base.tar, while confirming obsolete.txt, route.txt, and deletions.txt were absent. The resulting tree contained only the expected two files and remained correct after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-91c1a728dd4b4061","cmd-90e5542036c44d94","cmd-46ee13fbd3244c0c","cmd-a1a6da89d2d5481c"]},{"id":"preserve_media_and_order","requirement":"Preserve all recovery media and the archive order documented in chain.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"chain.txt retained the order base.tar, day2.tar, day3.tar. SHA-256 hashes for all three archives and chain.txt matched the preparation baseline before reconstruction, afterward, and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-52a59889c140407a","cmd-ccb4c0abd2104db9","cmd-46ee13fbd3244c0c","cmd-a1a6da89d2d5481c"]},{"id":"retain_platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 before and after execution. Reconstruction used existing standard platform utilities, with no package or platform change observed and package health remaining clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-52a59889c140407a","cmd-a1a6da89d2d5481c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. cmd-90e5542036c44d94 created the required recovered tree, applied required deletions, and cleaned its temporary staging directory. cmd-49f95625b7824090 scheduled the mandatory provider restart through transient systemd units, which did not remain after reboot. All other commands were read-only verification or bounded diagnostics. Lifecycle evidence shows no failed services, damaged package state, new exposure, or abandoned temporary artifacts. The restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state and identity, restart acknowledgement, a changed post-restart identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, data, media, and network state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-90e5542036c44d94","cmd-46ee13fbd3244c0c","cmd-49f95625b7824090","cmd-e824b89b0636456d","cmd-a1a6da89d2d5481c","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. The recovered workspace accurately represents end of day 3, source media and ordering were preserved byte-for-byte, and the operating-system release and kernel were retained. The separate mandatory node-restart protocol was also fully demonstrated, including successful post-restart recovery.","limitations":[]}
